  skos:description "A Quality Measure Name is a designation used to identify and label a specific quality measure within a certification context. It serves as the official title by which a measure is recognized, enabling clear reference and communication in quality assessment and certification processes."@en ;
  schema:category "Trust|Certification|Service Quality and Security|List of Certifications: Quality and Security|Quality Measure Name" ;
